<h1>Maze application</h1>
<p>For tutorial purposes, we developed an application to act as a system under test - software under test, in
  this case - called <strong>Maze</strong>, which we'll use as the target of the tests we develop throughout this
  tutorial.</p>

<h2 id="download">Download</h2>
<p>We'll need all three versions later on in this tutorial. Create a <code>bin</code> folder with a subfolder per
  version, and download the executable matching your operating system into its version's subfolder:</p>
<ul>
  <li><a class="text-accent" href="https://github.com/GMCoreAI/orcraft-maze-app/releases/tag/maze-v1.0.0">1.0.0</a></li>
  <li><a class="text-accent" href="https://github.com/GMCoreAI/orcraft-maze-app/releases/tag/maze-v2.0.0">2.0.0</a></li>
  <li><a class="text-accent" href="https://github.com/GMCoreAI/orcraft-maze-app/releases/tag/maze-v3.0.0">3.0.0</a></li>
</ul>
<p>Each release provides a Windows, Linux and macOS executable, so the result looks like this (keep only the one
  matching your operating system):</p>
{{ codeblock.block('bin/
  v1.0.0/
    maze-v1.0.0-win.exe
    maze-v1.0.0-linux
    maze-v1.0.0-macos
  v2.0.0/
    maze-v2.0.0-win.exe
    maze-v2.0.0-linux
    maze-v2.0.0-macos
  v3.0.0/
    maze-v3.0.0-win.exe
    maze-v3.0.0-linux
